{"title":"1971 AHSME Problems/Problem 33","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Answer_Choices)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Answer Choices)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Answer_Choices)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Answer Choices)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Correction_by_Dr._Xue&#39;s_Math_School\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Correction by Dr. Xue's Math School</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Problems/Problem_33&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the product of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> quantities in Geometric Progression, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> their sum, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/3/bf344aa376979a8a81e8784f92fcb2381897ba65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S&#39;$\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> the sum of their reciprocals, \nthen <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> in terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/d/f9d093f48be277660500c385a3bc69061510c552.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S, S&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"35\" height=\"17\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/d/10ddc53b181c4fa3b1266d50dc20b05c0ad69712.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }(SS&#39;)^{\\frac{1}{2}n}\\qquad \\textbf{(B) }(S/S&#39;)^{\\frac{1}{2}n}\\qquad \\textbf{(C) }(SS&#39;)^{n-2}\\qquad \\textbf{(D) }(S/S&#39;)^n\\qquad \\textbf{(E) }(S/S&#39;)^{\\frac{1}{2}(n-1)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"668\" height=\"24\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Problems/Problem_33&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Geometric_sequence\" title=\"Geometric sequence\">geometric sequence</a> have first term <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and common ratio <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Then, the first <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> terms of the sequence are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/2/0c2cfebd99ff5ba76a199d9a20cc692d97640b34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,aR,aR^2,\\ldots,aR^{n-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"172\" height=\"20\" />. The product of these terms <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/8/b882ecfddd05c6aff6ed6447c2ce94960df7f612.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^nR^{1+2+\\ldots+n-1}=a^nR^{\\frac{(n-1)n}2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"216\" height=\"21\" /> by the formula for <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Triangular_numbers\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Triangular numbers\">triangular numbers</a>. Using the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Geometric_sequence#Sum\" title=\"Geometric sequence\">sum formula</a> reveals that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/9/b69a00f07eba9fc897e20bd2c1feb0d589a41164.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S=a\\cdot\\frac{1-R^n}{1-R}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"119\" height=\"41\" />.\n</p><p>We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/4/e64540440001913b335500c2ab1e026a28ba46ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S^{\\prime}=\\tfrac1a+\\tfrac1{aR}+\\ldots+\\tfrac1{aR^{n-1}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"207\" height=\"23\" /> Combining fractions reveals that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/8/338cec6c24ed2051edf8665b35541f017881d3c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S^{\\prime}=\\frac{aR^{n-1}+aR^{n-2}+\\ldots+aR+a}{a^2R^{n-1}}=\\frac S{a^2R^{n-1}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"375\" height=\"41\" />. Note that this denominator looks suspiciously similar to our formula for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. In fact, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/5/1b5fa16d057a45019988401d6e346ec865855589.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a^2+R^{n-1})^{\\frac n2}=a^n+R^{\\frac{(n-1)n}2}=P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"268\" height=\"26\" />. Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/b/c5baebb4adee9db07f4a2135f7adff16aa561827.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(S/S^{\\prime})^{\\frac n2}=(a^2+R^{n-1})^{\\frac n2}=P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"233\" height=\"22\" />, our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/e/00e49416da08f56cc8d8b5ed74aab28d4a03dcef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }(S/S^{\\prime})^{\\frac 12n}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"118\" height=\"35\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Answer_Choices.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Answer_Choices)\">Solution 2 (Answer Choices)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Problems/Problem_33&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Answer Choices)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can just look at a very specific case: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/0/ed095eb0aeee85e763181d09580a4c351838a60d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1, 2, 4, 8.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"64\" height=\"16\" /> Here, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/2/4025f673d0ca464ffb4a2f213f22fad51304940b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=4, P=64, S=15,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"175\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/6/856b3daa423ccfb08bfdce3ccee58353b1ae7363.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S&#39;=\\frac{30}{16}=\\frac{15}{8}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"113\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Then, plug in values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/d/1ad5a9a921f0393d3c8f15c19fecce57292421ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S, S&#39;,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"40\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> into each of the answer choices and see if it matches the product. \n</p><p>Answer choice <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/3/5b3a292f4ed36ec6630e7e7a4794408855bc24c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }(S/S&#39;)^{\\frac{1}{2}n}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"118\" height=\"35\" /> works: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/5/d551328397b9747c5b834603ba1c4ab4d1172faf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\frac{15}{\\frac{15}{8}})^2 = 64.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"89\" height=\"44\" />\n</p><p>-edited by coolmath34\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Answer_Choices.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Answer_Choices)\">Solution 3 (Answer Choices)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Problems/Problem_33&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Answer Choices)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can use <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Dimensional_analysis&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Dimensional analysis (page does not exist)\">dimensional analysis</a> to cut down our answer choices. Suppose that each of the terms in the geometric progression is in units of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/8/eb8795e92ca0e569a698bea358b31099d842242d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{meters}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"12\" />. Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> should have units of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/8/eb8795e92ca0e569a698bea358b31099d842242d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{meters}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/3/163f679cbeaa77df38c51e0e4d9be88343d076ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S^{\\prime}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"16\" /> units of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/8/0287e24dc57dd3dc68e4550341c058e837e46495.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac1{\\text{meters}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"44\" height=\"23\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> units of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/d/e2dc61bbc449c7144fead93d74359c0033ebcbc7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{meters}^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"59\" height=\"14\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/b/22b9c55b82e0ddff082a56cb17458d43735fdb5a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$SS^{\\prime}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"16\" /> is unitless, so we can eliminate options (A) and (C). <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/b/7bb3c1e9f62c3a83141fdbf9c17f3c0838c89db1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S/S^{\\prime}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"20\" /> has units <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/9/de95ffda2321d522dd733a5c5951a6c75c130805.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{meters}^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"17\" />, so, to equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> (which has units <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/d/e2dc61bbc449c7144fead93d74359c0033ebcbc7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{meters}^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"59\" height=\"14\" />), the exponent needs to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/d/8ad4db0a3329e76fe3f6ac403fc6a05cce4ec485.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac n2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"14\" height=\"20\" />. The only remaining answer choice which satsifies this constraint is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/6513a2e008bb6add63b3470b8d2c86316f3ea412.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }(S/S^{\\prime})^{\\frac12n}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"118\" height=\"35\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Correction_by_Dr._Xue.27s_Math_School\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Correction_by_Dr._Xue's_Math_School\">Video Correction by Dr. Xue's Math School</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Problems/Problem_33&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Correction by Dr. Xue&#39;s Math School\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>This problem is WRONG. A counterexample is given in the video:\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/0HSKE4ZC_8Y\">https://youtu.be/0HSKE4ZC_8Y</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Problems/Problem_33&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME\" title=\"1971 AHSME\">1971 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1971 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1971 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1971\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Problems/Problem_32\" title=\"1971 AHSME Problems/Problem 32\">Problem 32</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Problems/Problem_34\" title=\"1971 AHSME Problems/Problem 34\">Problem 34</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1971 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1971 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1971 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php